Yes. The diff changes the Meet fallback check from optional chaining to an unguarded dereference:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
```

If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `undefined`, `null`, or an empty array, destructuring yields `mainHostDestinationCalendar === undefined`, and accessing `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw a `TypeError`. Because this expression is evaluated whenever `evt.location === MeetLocationType` (due to `&&` short-circuit), it can crash Meet bookings when no destination calendar is set. Previously `evt.destinationCalendar?.integration` avoided this.
